	<section class="section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
		<div class="section__inner section__inner--split">
			<div>
				<p class="section__kicker">About Fanziquan</p>
				<h2 id="about-title">One of the oldest schools of Chinese martial arts</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>Fanziquan is one of the oldest schools within Chinese martial arts.</p>
				<p>The Fanziquan practiced at Northeastern Lineage Fanzimen belongs to the northeastern Chinese tradition and follows the lineage of Yu Boqian, who learned from the Three Elders of Fengtian.</p>
				<p>Fanziquan is built primarily on hand techniques. Its defining qualities are firecracker-like rapid combinations and overwhelming power. It does not rely on difficult, ornamental movements; its fighting method is centered on the hands. Its few kicking techniques are practical, easy to learn, and support the hand techniques well.</p>
				<p>The appeal of Fanziquan lies in using overwhelming speed and power to seize the initiative and finish the attack at once. This does not mean swinging the arms blindly.</p>
				<p>Speed and power beyond ordinary athletic ability are produced by precise body mechanics. Through the study of human structure and efficient movement, Fanziquan reaches a level of speed and force that would otherwise seem impossible.</p>
				<p>With serious practice, one can aim to develop formidable ability within three to five years.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section--dark" aria-labelledby="features-title">
		<div class="section__inner">
			<p class="section__kicker">Three Features</p>
			<h2 id="features-title">Fast, powerful, practical</h2>
			<div class="feature-grid">
				<article class="feature">
					<h3>Fast</h3>
					<p>Fanziquan attacks with hand combinations like firecrackers, leaving no time for the opponent to react. One strike does not end the attack; the hands continue in rapid succession.</p>
				</article>
				<article class="feature">
					<h3>Powerful</h3>
					<p>It shocks the opponent with overwhelming power and takes control. Speed is important, but so is the strong issuing force developed through fundamentals.</p>
				</article>
				<article class="feature">
					<h3>Practical</h3>
					<p>Because it is built mainly on hand techniques, Fanziquan is easy to approach and highly practical. It avoids decorative complexity and focuses on methods directly tied to offense and defense.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" id="reason" aria-labelledby="reason-title">
		<div class="section__inner">
			<p class="section__kicker">Strength and Learnability</p>
			<h2 id="reason-title">Simple enough to be strong, structured enough to learn</h2>
			<div class="practice-list">
				<article>
					<h3>Not dependent on one strike</h3>
					<p>The strength of Fanziquan lies in simple continuous attack. It does not rely on a single blow, and it does not stop after one strike.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>It denies the opponent their chance</h3>
					<p>Fanziquan closes distance from long range and overwhelms with repeated attacks before the opponent can reset or show their true ability.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Less dependent on luck</h3>
					<p>It does not depend on delicate or obscure techniques. By overwhelming with speed and power, it is less likely to be decided by chance.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>A clear training system</h3>
					<p>The curriculum is organized so that students can progress step by step and acquire the art in a structured way.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Only three routines</h3>
					<p>Yu Boqian organized the Fanziquan he learned from the Three Elders of Fengtian into three routines: beginner, intermediate, and advanced. This lets students focus on usable practice rather than memorizing endless sequences.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>No distracting branches</h3>
					<p>Many Chinese martial arts contain many decorative branches. They can be fun, but they often make learning harder. Fanziquan lets students focus on the core.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Direct frontal pressure</h3>
					<p>It does not rely on difficult footwork to circle to the opponent's side. It drives in from the front, seeking to surpass the opponent physically and suppress them with speed and power.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Less dependence on flexibility</h3>
					<p>Because it is hand-centered, with few high kicks and few extremely low stances, it is approachable even for people who are not confident in leg flexibility.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
			<p class="note">Many techniques are simple, making Fanziquan a realistic art even for people who are not naturally athletic or coordinated.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" id="school" aria-labelledby="school-title">
		<div class="section__inner section__inner--split">
			<div>
				<p class="section__kicker">About Northeastern Lineage Fanzimen</p>
				<h2 id="school-title">Preserving pure Fanziquan without mixture</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>Northeastern Lineage Fanzimen is a traditional martial arts group dedicated to practicing Fanziquan in the Yu Boqian lineage.</p>
				<p>We preserve pure Fanziquan without mixture, pursuing its original methods, body mechanics, and applications through fundamental training.</p>
				<p>The Fanziquan often seen in modern performance competition is performance Fanziquan based on Tongbei boxing's Fanziquan. Tongbei boxing's Fanziquan itself is also based on the northeastern Fanziquan learned by the brothers Ma Fengtu and Ma Yingtu.</p>
				<p>Because Fanziquan is an old school with many branches, we use the name Northeastern Lineage to distinguish our practice from other branches.</p>
				<p>Our purpose is not competition or performance. We value traditional body mechanics, fundamentals, methods, and applications, and we train step by step to preserve Fanziquan for the next generation.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" id="practice" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
		<div class="section__inner">
			<p class="section__kicker">Practice Content</p>
			<h2 id="practice-title">From fundamentals to routines, single methods, and applications</h2>
			<div class="practice-list">
				<article>
					<h3>Body Building</h3>
					<p>Fanziquan values a body that can actually move. We train stamina, issuing power, posture, and body mechanics to support continuous hand combinations.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Fundamentals</h3>
					<p>Everyone, from beginners to advanced practitioners, practices martial fundamentals. Even experienced Chinese martial artists begin with the basics in our group.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Routines</h3>
					<p>Yu Boqian organized Fanziquan into three routines: beginner, intermediate, and advanced. Through routines, students learn methods, movement flow, and the rhythm of combination striking.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Single Methods</h3>
					<p>We extract individual techniques from the routines and train hand methods, issuing power, footwork, and distance.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Applications</h3>
					<p>Applications show how the movements from routines and single methods work in actual offense and defense.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Partner Practice</h3>
					<p>Practice is adjusted according to experience, whether the student is new to fighting, new to Chinese martial arts, or already experienced.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
			<p class="note">Fanziquan is physically demanding, and practice is quiet, focused, and sweaty. However, we do not force unsafe training.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section--muted" id="target" aria-labelledby="target-title">
		<div class="section__inner section__inner--split">
			<div>
				<p class="section__kicker">Who Can Join</p>
				<h2 id="target-title">An open entrance, serious practice</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>Both beginners and experienced martial artists may participate. Even those with Chinese martial arts experience begin with martial fundamentals in our group.</p>
				<p>People who simply want exercise or who just want to try Fanziquan once are also welcome. First, experience its movement, power, and depth. Those who then wish to study Fanziquan seriously as a traditional martial art are welcome.</p>
				<p>Fanziquan is a physically demanding school. For people without exercise experience, around age forty is a rough guideline. Individual fitness varies, so please contact us if you would like to participate.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" id="safety" aria-labelledby="safety-title">
		<div class="section__inner section__inner--split">
			<div>
				<p class="section__kicker">Safety Policy</p>
				<h2 id="safety-title">Practice without injury</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>At Northeastern Lineage Fanzimen, we value practice without injury.</p>
				<p>We do not force excessive training. Practice is adjusted according to each person's fitness and ability, and beginners are not suddenly pushed into high-intensity work.</p>
				<p>In partner practice especially, harsh or bullying behavior by seniors toward juniors is never allowed.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

