	<section class="section section--muted" id="teacher" aria-labelledby="teacher-title">
		<div class="section__inner section__inner--split">
			<div>
				<p class="section__kicker">Representative Profile</p>
				<h2 id="teacher-title">Tomoaki Nagahara</h2>
				<div class="teacher-stats">
					<p>30 years in Chinese martial arts</p>
					<p>All Japan Wushu Taijiquan Championships winner</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>As a child, he grew up watching Jackie Chan films and became interested in Chinese martial arts.</p>
				<p>After becoming an adult, he read in a Chinese martial arts magazine that if one wished to master striking, one needed to study Fanziquan. That sentence caught his eye and made him want to learn it.</p>
				<p>He was drawn to Fanziquan's rapid combinations, and because it is centered on hand techniques, he felt that even someone without natural athletic talent could learn it.</p>
				<p>Through practice, he became deeply attracted to its learnability, practicality, and ability to control an opponent through overwhelming movement.</p>
				<p>What appeals to him is that Fanziquan does not lean on complicated, obscure tricks, but overwhelms through speed, power, and continuous technical attack.</p>
				<p>At first, he began training casually, thinking of it as light exercise once a week. Over time, however, Fanziquan and Chinese martial arts became a major purpose in his life.</p>
				<p>In addition to Fanziquan and Chuojiao, he is versed in Changquan, Yiquan, Xingyiquan, Piguaquan, Tanglangquan, Tongbeiquan, and Choy Li Fut. In Changquan, Piguaquan, and Xingyiquan, he is among the top practitioners in Japan. He also studies and practices boxing, Muay Thai, Kali, and Silat.</p>
				<p>In teaching, he adjusts practice according to each person's ability and aptitude, emphasizing steady progress. Even complete beginners are guided from fundamentals toward acquiring Fanziquan methods.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
		<div class="section__inner">
			<p class="section__kicker">Q&amp;A</p>
			<h2 id="faq-title">Before You Join</h2>
			<div class="faq-list">
				<details>
					<summary>Can beginners join?</summary>
					<p>Yes. Our goal is to train beginners into skilled practitioners. We begin with martial fundamentals and build the body and methods of Fanziquan step by step.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Is there an age limit?</summary>
					<p>Fanziquan is physically demanding. For those without exercise experience, around forty is a general guideline. Fitness varies, so please contact us if you wish to participate.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Is it okay if I am not confident in my fitness?</summary>
					<p>Practice is adjusted according to each person's ability. We do not suddenly put people through high-intensity training.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can experienced martial artists join?</summary>
					<p>Yes. Practitioners of other combat sports or other schools may join. Regardless of experience, however, everyone begins with martial fundamentals in our group.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I learn Chuojiao?</summary>
					<p>Chuojiao instruction is possible. However, because our main focus is Fanziquan, it is taught after the student's Fanziquan has reached a certain level.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I learn weapons of Fanzimen?</summary>
					<p>Northeastern Lineage Fanzimen preserves Landao and Zuoba spear. Weapons instruction is possible for those who wish to learn it.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>What happens in trial practice?</summary>
					<p>Please join a regular practice session and try the same practice as the other participants. The content is mainly Fanziquan fundamentals and body-building practice.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I only observe?</summary>
					<p>Observation-only visits are not currently accepted. Since you have the opportunity, please experience the practice itself.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Do I need a reservation for trial practice?</summary>
					<p>Yes. Trial practice requires advance reservation. Walk-ins are not accepted, and either the Roppongi or Nerima practice may be chosen.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How much does participation cost?</summary>
					<p>Participation uses a ticket system. A 10-session ticket costs 10,000 yen. Facility fees are charged at actual cost.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>What should I wear or bring?</summary>
					<p>Wear clothes suitable for exercise and bring indoor shoes, a towel, and water. Martial arts shoes are not required.</p>
				</details>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

